### Architecture source of truth

[`CLAUDE.md`](./CLAUDE.md) is the authoritative architecture doc (build
commands, conventions, CI/CD, tech stack). When this README and `CLAUDE.md`
disagree, `CLAUDE.md` wins and this README needs updating.

### AI tooling

This repo supports multi-AI contributions. Tool-specific entrypoints
(`.cursorrules`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md` if present) defer to
[`CLAUDE.md`](./CLAUDE.md) on disagreement. See
[`ai/AI_TEAM_PLAYBOOK.md`](./ai/AI_TEAM_PLAYBOOK.md) for multi-tool
coordination conventions.

### Operating modes

This repo supports two AI-assisted contribution rhythms (see
[`repo-standards`](https://github.com/Ranzlappen/repo-standards) PROMPT.md
rules 13–14). Both rhythms are preceded by **Phase 0 — Migration Planning**
([`prompt/migration-planning.md`](https://github.com/Ranzlappen/repo-standards/blob/main/prompt/migration-planning.md)),
which produces a repo profile, a must/should/could/skip score of the
checklist, and a resumable batch roadmap before any commits land.

- **Default — Canonical 8-PR sequence** for full upgrade passes.
- **Alternative — Single Feature Branch / Single PR** for focused work
  that would otherwise produce ≤3 PRs (open a draft early, subscribe to
  PR activity, commits accumulate on the branch, ready-for-review at
  completion).

Out-of-scope findings auto-file a GitHub issue (label
`out-of-scope,from-claude`) by default; opt out per-repo by setting
`DISABLE_OUT_OF_SCOPE_ISSUES=true` in repository variables.

### Behavior preservation (non-negotiable)

Any AI-driven or human contribution against this repo follows
[`repo-standards`](https://github.com/Ranzlappen/repo-standards) `PROMPT.md`
rule 2: keep **100% of original functionality**, analyze the repo *before*
editing, and flag **repo-specific risks / edge-cases** in every PR
description and post-task self-check. "None observed" is acceptable; the
heading must be present.

